NNAAMMEE
     ssyyssmmeerrggee — update system configuration files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssyyssmmeerrggee [--bbddpp]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssyyssmmeerrggee is a utility designed to help the administrator update configu‐
     ration files after upgrading to a new release or snapshot.

     ssyyssmmeerrggee works by comparing a reference root directory against currently
     installed files.

     ssyyssmmeerrggee will work through the fileset, offering the chance to merge any
     differences using sdiff(1).  Merged files may be edited using the default
     editor or be left to deal with at a later date.  Should any problems oc‐
     cur, such as a failure to upgrade a file, the user will be notified and
     will have to deal with the issue by hand.

     By default (if --dd is not used) ssyyssmmeerrggee only compares files whose refer‐
     ence sources have changed since the last run and attempts to automati‐
     cally upgrade them to the newest version, provided that they have no lo‐
     cal changes.  It automatically installs missing files and binaries, and
     updates files differing only by CVS Id.  Files whose reference sources
     have matching CVS Id are skipped from comparison.  _/_e_t_c_/_f_b_t_a_b and
     _/_e_t_c_/_t_t_y_s are created using helper scripts and are aallwwaayyss compared.
     Users and groups that are missing from the current installation but
     present in the new master.passwd(5) and group(5) files will aallwwaayyss be au‐
     tomatically (re)created.

     ssyyssmmeerrggee will finish by running mtree(8) to make sure the directory
     structure has correct permissions.

     The options are as follows:

     --bb      Batch mode.  ssyyssmmeerrggee runs non-interactively, saving differing
             files for later manual processing.

     --dd      Diff mode.  ssyyssmmeerrggee does not take any automatic action, allowing
             for a full diff comparison.

     --pp      Package mode.  ssyyssmmeerrggee only compares the default configuration
             files of installed packages(7) against their target on the system
             (@sample).

